  "stem": "If \\(x^{2} + 6x + 9 = 25\\) and \\(x > 0\\), what is the value of \\(x\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "2"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The left side is a perfect square: \\((x + 3)^{2} = 25\\).",
    "So \\(x + 3 = 5\\) or \\(x + 3 = -5\\), giving \\(x = 2\\) or \\(x = -8\\). Since \\(x > 0\\), \\(x = 2\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
